mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> as shown in the figure. If the first minimum is detected at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, the value of slits separation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;will be :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1aa042d7-3e08-4c80-a366-e1c6d2bf4a87-9894890.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 197px;\" /></p><p>The distance of screen from slits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7848cb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec976"}, {"id": "07267d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec977"}, {"id": "8607af", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec978"}, {"id": "491991", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec979"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538323"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52a5"], "question": {"text": "In a Young's double slit experiment, the path difference, at a certain point on the screen, betwen two interfering waves is $\\frac{1}{8}$ th of wavelength. The ratio of the intensity at this point to that at the centre of a bright fringe is close to:"}, "options": [{"id": "150e1c", "text": "0.74", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97b"}, {"id": "ec2ae5", "text": "0.85", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97c"}, {"id": "7463de", "text": "0.94", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97d"}, {"id": "72279a", "text": "0.8", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec97f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538323"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4ef4"], "question": {"text": "The width of one of the two slits in a Young's double slit experiment is 4 times that of the other slit. The ratio of the maximum of the minimum intensity in the interference pattern is:"}, "options": [{"id": "929501", "text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec980"}, {"id": "5192f9", "text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec981"}, {"id": "46a3bd", "text": "$9: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec982"}, {"id": "3b48ee", "text": "$16: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec983"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:27:59.559Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:27:59.559Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9ca"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9c8", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9ac", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538323"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4ef4"], "question": {"text": "In a Young&#39;s double slit experiment, an angular width of the fringe is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> on a screen placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away for particular wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>. The angular width of the fringe, when whole system is immersed in a medium of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "2ba0e5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9ad"}, {"id": "0e2f7f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9ae"}, {"id": "ab01a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9af"}, {"id": "15ba68", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927c"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b5"], "question": {"text": "Two waves of intensity ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>9</mn></math> cross each other at a point. The resultant intensities at the point, when (a) Waves are incoherent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced></math>  Waves are coherent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and differ in phase by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math> _________."}, "options": [{"id": "6f4a97", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b2"}, {"id": "b489fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b3"}, {"id": "eb4aec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b4"}, {"id": "02d57a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee8"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5dfa"], "question": {"text": "The difference in the number of waves when&nbsp;yellow light propagates through air and vacuum columns of the same thickness is one. The thickness of the air column is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mm</mi></math>. [Refractive index of air <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0003</mn></math>, the wavelength of yellow light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "864382", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b7"}, {"id": "dd4bfc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b8"}, {"id": "cade10", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9b9"}, {"id": "1810a0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9ba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9bb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b63"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ef8"], "question": {"text": "<p>Unpolarised light is incident on the boundary between two dielectric media, whose dielectric constants are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> (medium &ndash;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> (medium &ndash; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>), respectively. To satisfy the condition, so that the reflected and refracted rays are perpendicular to each other, the angle of incidence should be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>,&nbsp;the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______.</p><p>(Given for dielectric media, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "adbb3f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9bc"}, {"id": "903d71", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9bd"}, {"id": "47c8ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9be"}, {"id": "045d07", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9bf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ec9c0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538323"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470d"], "question": {"text": "If the measured angular separation between the second minimum to the left of the central maximum and the third minimum to the right of the central maximum is $30^{\\circ}$ in a single slit 